      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ ذَبَحَ حَمَامَةً مِنْ حَمَامِ اَلْحَرَمِ قَالَ «عَلَيْهِ اَلْفِدَاءُ» قَالَ قُلْتُ فَيَأْكُلُهُ قَالَ «لاَ» قُلْتُ فَيَطْرَحُهُ قَالَ «إِذاً يَكُونُ عَلَيْهِ فِدَاءٌ آخَرُ» قَالَ قُلْتُ فَمَا يَصْنَعُ بِهِ قَالَ «يَدْفِنُهُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2356 - Ibn Abi Umayr narrated from Khallad, from Abu Abdullah (as), regarding a man who slaughtered a pigeon from the pigeons of the Haram.\nImam (as) said: \"He must offer an expiation (fidya).\"\nI asked: \"Can he eat it?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"No.\"\nI asked:\"Can he throw it away?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"If he does, another expiation will be required.\"\nI asked: \"Then what should he do with it?\"\nImam (as) said: \"He should bury it.\""
        ]
      }
    },
